Learners should know and understand the role and purpose of
promoting health and well-being across the lifespan:
•  Role – to raise awareness of health and well-being issues
•  Purpose – to increase an individual’s positive lifestyle choices
•  Benefits – to reduce risks to health and well-being and reduce

health and social care costs.

Learners should know and understand the following strategies that
may be used to support individuals to take responsibility for their
own health and well-being to include prevention and control:

•

key campaigns and current initiatives to raise awareness of health
and well-being issues with specific audiences at both local and
national level

•  educate by providing information and advice about health and

well-being to enable individuals to make positive lifestyle choices

•  encourage individuals to utilise their own strengths and their

informal networks.

